    st_gas_mustrun_p25_measured_level: { cell: "K", ev: "miso-172 ARM 2 — **KEEPER 2026-08-20-miso-172-p25mw**, promoted 2026-08-20 on the arm's OWN pre-registered gates (PREREG-miso172-p25-level-basis-2026-08-20.md, committed before either arm result was read), EVERY GATE PASSING, no owner override needed. A DROPPED-BASIS REPAIR WITH ZERO FREE PARAMETERS: p25_cf is a percentile of net/(nameplate x avail_mult) and thermal_tranche_p25_level reconstructed the floor as p25_cf x nameplate, dropping the avail_mult it was divided by, over-flooring every deep-derate plant by 1/avail_mult. THE CENSUS IS A PROOF, NOT AN ASSERTION: over all 134 MISO rows, 88 agree to within 0.1 % — exactly the plants with NO derate, where the two bases are algebraically identical — while 25 are >=1.10x, ALL derated (1402 2.594x, 1122 Ames 2.220x, 3459 Sabine 1.726x, 3457 1.249x). Nothing but a dropped avail_mult produces that split. Rule 23 satisfied WITHOUT touching the frozen deriver (zero bytes; pooled artifact NOT regenerated) — the new script IMPORTS the frozen online mask/net/derate/window. Rule 14 governs and is why this is a LEVEL repair and NEVER an exclusion. Rule 19: the level SOURCE is replaced; membership, window, mechanism id and the pmax x availability clip untouched. GATES: L-1 level exactness at unit grain (1122 73.26->33.00 MW, 1402 137.48->53.00, 3459 493.96->286.15, 3457 141.80->113.49; the three underated plants unmoved); L-2 liveness IN BAND all three years (-1.6964/-1.7245/-2.1946 TWh); L-3 Ames dispatch toward its own meter every year (+64.8/+74.5/+92.9 % over -> -17.6/-18.1/+3.1 %); K-3 ZERO new conduct failures; K-5 ZERO record-grain PASS->non-PASS flips over 67 records; K-6 shape held, 2024-25 IMPROVING (profile_r 0.947/0.961/0.981). C8: ST_GAS forced share 30.53/30.93/42.56 % -> 24.59/24.88/35.16 %, 2023 and 2024 BELOW the 30 % cap, criterion FAIL->PASS — the ONLY record change in the whole scorer output. Determination NOT-YET on C3a-2025 ALONE (was C3a-2025 + C8-2023). THE BLOCKER WAS CLEARED BY THE MECHANISM NOBODY EXPECTED: arm 1 attacked 1402's window head-on and did NOT clear it (zero-share 71.17->52.19 %, missing the 50 % rider by 2.2 pp); arm 2 never touches that window and clears C8 anyway, by taking the CLASS below budget so the provenance leg is never consulted. 1402's window defect is REAL and UNREPAIRED — no longer load-bearing, not bought off. LATENT AND NOT ARMED: the same defect reaches CC_REGULAR (max 2.03x) and CT_PEAKER (max 1.50x), inert at MISO because cc_mustrun_per_plant=False; arming that leg is a different mechanism under a different charter (rule 19), and the cross-ISO half is a per-ISO hand-off (rule 25). Evidence: results/calibration/RESULT-miso172-p25-level-basis-2026-08-20.md; prereg PREREG-miso172-p25-level-basis-2026-08-20.md; runs 2026-08-20-miso-172-control / 2026-08-20-miso-172-p25mw; scorer scripts/probes/_miso172_window_ab.py." },
