    mustrun_plant_exclusions: { cell: "K", ev: "miso-170 KEEPER (PROMOTED 2026-08-19 BY OWNER DIRECTION over the session's own REJECTED-AS-ARMED mechanical verdict; both records stand): RESULT-miso170-stgas-floor-membership-2026-08-19.md; prereg PREREG-miso170-stgas-floor-membership-2026-08-19.md; runs 2026-08-19-miso-170-control / 2026-08-19-miso-170-membership; record _miso170_membership_ab.json. Armed WITH reliability_floor_plant_exclusions over ONE mechanism-blind CAMPD lay-up census (15 of 62 covered plants at 18/18 zero cells, nearest non-qualifier 16/18), which selects 7 of the 8 D-4-flagged plants blind to any D-4 verdict. Against the designated keeper the arm differs in EXACTLY ONE of 67 scorer records and it is an IMPROVEMENT: C8 ST_GAS 2024 FAIL -> PASS, the first MISO year ever to clear C8's provenance leg. K-0 bit-identity 12/12 max|diff|=0.0; K-2 shed 0.5295/0.8653/0.9459 TWh inside the pre-registered +/-50% band; K-3 conduct failures 18 -> 3 with ZERO new; K-5 zero flips; K-6 shape held; ZERO DOF (n_residual unchanged at 2). K-1 (membership exactness) FAILED AS WRITTEN on two residual plant-1104 reliability_floor rows and is RECORDED, NOT REWRITTEN - the unit-grain forensic shows 1104's ST_GAS rows carry ZERO reliability-floor unit-hours and the residual is 777/763 unit-hours on its CT_PEAKER tranches inside h15-21, charged to ST_GAS because aggregate_floors_by_plant labels a plant with its most common unit group. That D-4 INSTRUMENT ATTRIBUTION DEFECT affects any ISO with mixed-class sites and is an OPEN owner item. DO NOT extend the census to clear it (rules 1/14): plant 1402 Little Gypsy is a CYCLER (6/18 cells, P(on)=0.506) whose 2023 forcing is a WINDOW defect - pooled online_frac 0.508 vs per-year metered 0.2495/0.6134/0.6548 - and is the NAMED SUCCESSOR, not a membership candidate. Determination UNCHANGED at NOT-YET (C3a-2025 + C8 2023/2025)" },
